==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|firlazzan|firlāzzan|lang=goh}}, equivalent to {{prefix|ver|lassen|t1=for-|t2=let, leave|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fɛɐ̯ˈlasn̩/|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|ver|las|sen}}
* {{audio|De-verlassen.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|verlässt|verließ|verlassen}}

# {{context|intransitive}} to [[leave]], to [[abandon]]; to [[depart]], to [[forsake]]
#: ''Die Ratten '''verlassen''' das sinkende Schiff.'' — The rats are abandoning the sinking ship.
#: ''Er '''verließ''' das Haus um 7 Uhr.'' — He left the house at 7 o'clock.
# {{context|transitive|reflexive|''with'' "[[auf]]"}} to [[trust]]; to [[rely on]]
#: ''Ich '''verlasse mich''' dar'''auf''', dass du morgen da bist.'' — I trust you that you will be there tomorrow.
#: ''Ich '''habe''' mich sehr auf deine Informationen '''verlasen'''!'' — I did rely a lot upon your infomation!
# {{context|intransitive|figuratively}} to [[pass away]]; to [[cease]]; to [[die]]
#: ''Es tut mir leid, aber deine Mutter '''hat''' uns gestern Nacht '''verlassen'''.'' — I am sorry, but your mother passed away last night.
# {{context|intransitive}} to [[desert]], to [[dump]] (''e.g.: a relationship'')
#: ''Nach einer dreijährigen Beziehung '''verließ''' sie ihn.'' — After three years of an affectionate relationship, she dumped him.

